To determine if the password is symmetric with respect to the central button of the terminal, we need to check if the input matrix is symmetric about its center. 
The given matrix is a 3x3 grid where 'X' represents a pressed button and '.' represents an unpressed button.
The central symmetry means that for every 'X' or '.' at position (i, j), there should be the same character at the position (2-i, 2-j) because the matrix is 0-indexed.
We will iterate over the matrix and check for central symmetry by comparing characters at corresponding symmetric positions.
If we find any pair of characters that are not the same, we immediately conclude that the matrix is not symmetric and output 'NO'.
