To solve this problem, we first need to identify all prime numbers up to the given number n. 
We will create a list of prime numbers using the Sieve of Eratosthenes algorithm. 
Once we have the list of primes, we will iterate through the list to find pairs of neighboring primes. 
For each pair of neighboring primes, we will calculate the sum of the two primes plus one and check if this sum is also a prime number within the given range. 
We will count how many prime numbers can be expressed in this form. 
