4. For an odd n*m, we can pair up the squares into (n*m - 1)/2 pairs of adjacent squares (since one square is the capital and not to be revisited until the end). The teleporter can be used to jump between two squares of the same color that are not too far apart, effectively creating a path that allows the king to visit all squares.

5. The minimum number of teleporters required is either 0 (if n*m is even) or 1 (if n*m is odd), as we can plan the path such that only one teleporter is needed to make the journey feasible.

