2. When we encounter a double quote, we will toggle a flag that indicates whether we are currently inside a quoted lexeme or not. 
3. If we are inside a quoted lexeme, we will keep adding characters to the current lexeme until we encounter another double quote.
4. If we are not inside a quoted lexeme and we encounter a non-space character, we will start building a new lexeme.
5. After iterating through the entire string, we will add the last lexeme to our list if it is not empty.
